{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"77078c3d-af14-44b9-852a-1dcb1af0dee6","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The causes of the failure and the fix have been determined and documented.\n\n### Root Causes\n1. **Silent Crash in Notification Logic (`status` is read-only in Zsh)**:\n   In [`bin/nightly-review.zsh`](file:///tmp/h-eGbZXn/bin/nightly-review.zsh#L19), the script executed `status=$?`. In Zsh, `status` is a built-in read-only alias for `$?`. Attempting to assign to it throws a fatal error (`read-only variable: status`), causing the script to abort immediately before reaching the failure branch where [`bin/notify.sh`](file:///tmp/h-eGbZXn/bin/notify.sh) would have sent an alert to Telegram.\n2. **Underlying Job Failure (`Not logged in · Please run /login`)**:\n   Under launchd's minimal runtime environment, environment variables such as `USER` are not automatically set. Claude Code inspects `process.env.USER` to query the macOS Keychain for credentials stored under the user's account name. Without `USER`, it fails to find the OAuth credentials and exits with code 1.\n\n### Fix\n- Modified [`bin/nightly-review.zsh`](file:///tmp/h-eGbZXn/bin/nightly-review.zsh#L18-L24) to rename `status` to `exit_code`, allowing error handling and failure reporting via `bin/notify.sh` to run properly.\n- Documented full details in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-eGbZXn/ANSWER.md).\n","duration_seconds":504.859036,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":406729,"output_tokens":12752,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":5879682,"total_tokens":419481}}}
